<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to July 2 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.44 (0.44)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.59 (0.58)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  1.04 (1.02)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.40 (0.39)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.54 (0.53)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.99 (0.98)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.35 (0.35)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.49 (0.48)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.26)	 three years  0.94 (0.93)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Jun 23 - Jun 27:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.61 (0.59)   120-150 days  0.69 (0.64)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.60 (0.59)   150-180 days  0.73 (0.71)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.62 (0.60)   180-360 days  0.73 (0.68)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.67 (0.62)   over 360 days 0.78 (0.88)</p>
